findings:
- finding_id: C1
  title: from_file_or_default swallows ALL errors including parse and permission failures
  weight: 8
  phase_ideal: dev
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: No phase identified that from_file_or_default swallows all errors. TEA
    tests config loading but none specifically test that parse/permission errors are
    distinguished from NotFound. Reviewer did not flag this.
- finding_id: I1
  title: CliError Display leaks internal details to stderr (CWE-209)
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: reviewer
  caught: true
  caught_by: dev
  evidence: "Dev implemented CWE-209 mitigation: ServerError display omits internal\
    \ details (error.rs:27), verified by reviewer. TEA also wrote exit_codes.rs tests\
    \ for CWE-209 security. However, the Display impl still uses eprintln directly\
    \ \u2014 the reviewer verified the Display sanitization but did not flag that\
    \ stderr still leaks via Io(transparent). Partial catch."
- finding_id: I2
  title: "SiemClient.tenant_id uses raw String \u2014 header injection risk (CWE-113)"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: tea
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: TEA wrote header injection tests for CWE-113 (newlines in tenant rejected
    via try_with_tenant), but SiemClient.tenant_id remains a raw String rather than
    using TenantId from axiathon-core. The type-safety gap was not flagged by any
    phase.
- finding_id: I3
  title: Dependencies use direct version strings instead of workspace = true
  weight: 3
  phase_ideal: dev
  caught: true
  caught_by: reviewer
  evidence: 'Reviewer flagged [MEDIUM]: ''clap_complete, comfy-table, csv, dirs, keyring,
    reqwest, toml are declared with inline versions instead of workspace = true, despite
    existing in [workspace.dependencies]. This creates version drift risk.'''
- finding_id: I4
  title: "Config token field silently ignored \u2014 secret left on disk"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: reviewer
  caught: true
  caught_by: reviewer
  evidence: 'Reviewer flagged [MEDIUM]: ''No #[serde(deny_unknown_fields)]. An operator
    who writes token = "my-secret" in cli.toml gets zero feedback that the field is
    ignored.'' TEA also wrote config_file_with_token_field_is_rejected_or_ignored
    test but reviewer noted the test ''explicitly accepts both behaviors (reject or
    ignore), masking this gap.'''
- finding_id: I5
  title: "Vacuously true test \u2014 assertion is None || true"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: tea
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: No phase identified the vacuously true assertion pattern (is_none() ||
    ...). TEA wrote config_loading tests but did not flag this specific assertion
    logic flaw.
- finding_id: I6
  title: "Test with zero assertions \u2014 only checks non-panic"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: tea
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: No phase identified a test with zero assertions that only checks non-panic
    via 'let _ = config'. TEA wrote config tests but this specific zero-assertion
    test was not flagged.
